---
import danHeadshot from "../images/headshots/dan-avatar.png";
import marinaHeadshot from "../images/headshots/Marina-Levy-Headshot.png";
import kyleHeadshot from "../images/headshots/kyle-coberly-headshot.jpg";
import Avatar from "../components/Avatar.astro";
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import Icon from "../components/Icon.astro";
import { proof } from "../data/services";
---

<Layout
  title="About | 17th Street Labs"
  description="17th Street Labs is an applied AI engineering studio in Denver, New York City, and Boston. Meet the engineers who do the work."
>
  <section class="page-hero">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="chip">About</p>
      <h1 class="statement">The demo is the easy part.</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        17th Street Labs is an applied AI engineering studio. We build evals,
        agents, and architectures for production, and we measure everything
        we ship.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="band">
    <div class="wrap">
      <dl class="proof">
        {proof.map(({ value, label }) => (
          <div>
            <dt>{value}</dt>
            <dd>{label}</dd>
          </div>
        ))}
      </dl>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="band">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="band-head">
        <p class="chip">Team</p>
        <h2 class="section-title">Senior people, one studio.</h2>
        <p>The people you meet are the people who do the work.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="founders">
        <article class="card founder">
          <Avatar src={marinaHeadshot} alt="Marina Levy" zoom={1.9} class="avatar-marina" />
          <div>
            <h3>Marina Levy</h3>
            <p class="role">Co-founder, chief executive officer</p>
            <p class="bio">
              Marina runs the studio. She turns ambitious technical work into
              engagements with a clear scope, a steady cadence, and an outcome
              we can be held to.
            </p>
          </div>
        </article>
        <article class="card founder">
          <Avatar src={danHeadshot} alt="Dan" />
          <div>
            <h3>Dan</h3>
            <p class="role">Founding Engineer</p>
            <p class="bio">
              Builds it, breaks it, measures it, builds it again. Dan asks the
              questions that decide whether a system is real: Can we prove it
              improved? What is the cheapest model that does the job? What
              changes when an attacker has the same leverage?
            </p>
          </div>
        </article>
        <article class="card founder">
          <Avatar src={kyleHeadshot} alt="Kyle" />
          <div>
            <h3>Kyle Coberly</h3>
            <p class="role">Head of Research</p>
            <p class="bio">
              Systems engineer and educator. At Urban Sky he shipped the flight
              simulation engine, stood up the company-wide testing stack, and
              built the tooling that lets AI agents work across every app in
              parallel. At Sunrun he led the rescue rewrite of the sales
              pipeline. Adjunct professor at the University of Denver and a
              seven-time Pluralsight Elite Instructor.
            </p>
          </div>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="band">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="band-head">
        <p class="chip">Principles</p>
        <h2 class="section-title">Ambitious and rigorous, at the same time.</h2>
        <p>
          AI should be part of the product, not a chatbot bolted on. And none
          of it matters if the thing does not work. We hold both.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="principles">
        <div class="card">
          <span class="card-icon"><Icon name="Gauge" /></span>
          <h3>Stop guessing. Start measuring.</h3>
          <p>
            “Seems better” is not a methodology. We measure what changed,
            find the failure, fix it, and prove the fix worked.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <span class="card-icon"><Icon name="ShieldCheck" /></span>
          <h3>The system is the product.</h3>
          <p>
            The model is one component. Architecture, harness, context, and
            tools decide the outcome. The best design often uses a smaller
            model.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <span class="card-icon"><Icon name="Zap" /></span>
          <h3>We experiment on ourselves first.</h3>
          <p>
            We spend our own money finding what fails and what works cheaply.
            What survives goes into client work, and your team leaves able to
            run it without us.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="band">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="closing">
        <h2 class="statement">Put it in front of engineers.</h2>
        <p>Send the system, not a brief. We will tell you what we would test first.</p>
        <div class="hero-actions">
          <a class="button button-solid" href="/contact/">
            Start a project
            <Icon name="ArrowRight" size={16} />
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
